## Known pre-existing failure (NOT caused by this task)
`node src/scripts/check-loam-ui.mjs` fails with `8 !== 7` on the
`assert.equal(await page.locator('#homeModes button').count(), 7)` line. Verified
pre-existing: `git stash push -u` of the entire fc-09 change set and re-running the gate on
the clean tree produces the identical `8 !== 7` assertion, and the gate only counts
home-page mode buttons, a file this task does not touch. It is a stale count in the gate
itself, not a regression from fc-09.

Also noted: `@testing-library/user-event` is not installed in `packages/web`, so the panel
test uses `fireEvent` from `@testing-library/react` instead.

## Self-review after the fact (interpretations and gaps)

Re-auditing the delivered work surfaced two things worth stating plainly.

**1. The `createEffectcraftExecutor` / `createRoundTripExecutor` are not yet consumed.**
A reference search confirms `createRoundTripExecutor` and `createEffectcraftExecutor`
appear only in `packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.ts` (the definitions) and in
`packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.test.ts` (the tests). Nothing constructs a
`VideoStudioClient` anywhere in `packages/web/src` yet, so no production code path reaches
the effects executor today. The interpretation I had to guess at: the task asked for these
executors, and the panel drives its round trip directly through the two bridge refs, so I
delivered the executors as the documented seam and tested them, rather than inventing a
wiring that no caller needs yet. If the intent was that agent `target: "effects"` commands
must be executable end to end, that wiring is still missing and is the next piece.

**2. `Done` is disabled rather than explained when there is no project.** I initially
"fixed" this by making `Done` show a notice when `projectPath` was null. A test I wrote for
that branch failed and disproved the premise: `openInEffects` always sets a derived path via
`effectsProjectPathFor(clip, taskId)`, so while the effects engine is showing, `projectPath`
is never null. The branch was unreachable dead code, so I reverted both the change and the
test. Current behaviour stands as delivered: `Done` is disabled (via `!projectPath`) and the
round trip reports failures through the notice banner.

**3. `openInEffects` trusts the panel's own project path.** It derives the path from the
clip and the task id rather than requiring the effects engine to confirm it saved. This is
consistent with `planRoundTrip`, which does the same, but it means a user-edited composition
is named by Loam rather than by the engine. Left as is deliberately: the engine's own
`inspect()` result takes precedence when it reports one.

Gates re-run after the reverts: web `tsc --noEmit` exit 0, touched web suites 12/12 pass,
working tree clean.

## Independent re-validation of fc-09 (post-completion)

Re-checked from scratch against the fc-09 acceptance criteria and the `.jtask.md` gates.
Everything below was run fresh in this worktree; nothing was taken on trust.

**1. Acceptance criteria (`.jtask.md`): "Unit with mocked film+effects bridges: full
round-trip command sequence; replace-in-place keeps neighbouring clips; reopen uses stored
.ecproj." All three are exercised and green.**

- Full round-trip sequence: `src/tools/__tests__/effectsRoundTrip.test.ts` "builds the full
  sequence: effects in, film replace out" asserts the exact 8-step target/method list
  (`effects:addFile -> execute(composition.new) -> execute(ask) -> execute(project.save)
  -> execute(renderQueue.render) -> readFile -> film:importFiles -> execute(timeline.replaceRange)`).
- Replace-in-place: "replaces the original range on the clip's own track" pins
  `{ clipId: "clip_b", trackId: "v1", fromSec: 10, toSec: 50 }`. Neighbouring-clip safety is
  the same mechanism plus the data-loss guard: `selectClip` refuses a clip id not on the
  timeline ("a wrong target is data loss"), and the timecode/selection parsers are tested.
- Reopen with the stored `.ecproj`: "plans openProject then inspect for a stored project"
  plus `effectsProjectPathFor` pinning the derived path. The panel covers the same path via
  `planReopenEffects` / `readEffectsProjectPath`.
- Executor safety: `packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.test.ts` proves an `effects`
  command can never be answered by the film bridge (and vice versa), and that the round-trip
  executor refuses an unknown target instead of dropping it.

**2. Gates (all six re-run fresh, all exit 0)**

| Gate | Command | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| root types | `npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |
| web types | `cd packages/web && npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |
| server build | `npm run build:server` | exit 0 (`pdf worker copied to dist/`) |
| web build | `cd packages/web && npx next build` | exit 0, 25/25 static pages |
| server tests | `node --import tsx --test <touched suites>` | 92 tests, 92 pass, 0 fail |
| web tests | `cd packages/web && npx vitest run` | 74 files, 479 tests, all pass |

Broader runs: the whole `src/tools/__tests__/*` + `videoStudioE2E` + `runTools` +
`riskTier` set gives 816 tests / 815 pass / 1 fail. The single failure is
`src/tools/__tests__/search.test.ts` "greps and globs the repository in under 1 second"
(`grep took 1149ms`) — a wall-clock perf budget in a suite fc-09 never touches, which failed
only because five builds/tests ran concurrently against it. Re-run in isolation: 19/19 pass,
exit 0. Not an fc-09 regression.

**3. Merge safety (both directions checked)**

- `git merge-tree --write-tree --messages HEAD manus-parity` -> **exit 0**. fc-09 merges
  cleanly into `manus-parity`; the branch is still 3 commits ahead of the base
  (`a8130cc`), and `manus-parity` has no `effectsRoundTrip.ts`, so the work is intact and
  unmerged.
- `git merge-tree --write-tree --messages HEAD khamis1992/cr-04` -> **exit 1**, conflicts in
  exactly `.jdone` and `packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.ts`. Confirmed by inspecting
  cr-04 (`4202a73`): it rewrites that client as
  `class VideoStudioClient extends RelayClientBase<VideoStudioTarget>` and keeps only
  `createFilmcraftExecutor` — `createEffectcraftExecutor` and `createRoundTripExecutor` are
  gone. A merge therefore needs a deliberate reconcile (keep the two fc-09 executors and
  adopt the shared relay base), not a blind resolution.

**4. Branding rule: verified, not assumed**

Every `FilmCraft` / `EffectCraft` / `ArtCraft` occurrence in `packages/web/src` is in code
identifiers or comments (4 hits across 3 files, none in a rendered string). The panel's
user-visible strings are exactly `Loam Video`, `Loam Effects`, `Open in effects`, `Done`,
`Loading` and one contextual notice. The panel test asserts both that the Loam labels render
and that `/EffectCraft/i` and `/FilmCraft/i` do not. `t()` falls back to the key when a
locale has no entry, so the Arabic catalog lacking the new keys renders the English source
string rather than an empty value or corrupted text.

**5. The wiring gap, adjudicated**

The gap reported in the earlier self-review is real but its severity was overstated in one
respect and understated in another, and the ownership is now clear.

- The fc-02 relay client (`packages/web/src/lib/videoStudioClient.ts`) was authored by the
  fc-02 task (commit `480bcc7`, merged into `manus-parity` on 2026-10-22 21:02) and never
  mounted there either. fc-09 extended it with the two effects executors. **The browser mount
  of the relay is an unfilled seam owned by fc-02, not introduced or required by fc-09.**
- Corrected claim: "nothing constructs a `VideoStudioClient`" is not evidence fc-09 shipped
  dead code. The panel's round trip runs directly through its two bridge refs
  (`bridgeRef`/`effectsBridgeRef`) and the shared planner, which is a complete and tested
  path. The executors are the *agent-relay* path's seam, and the existing E2E test
  (`src/server/__tests__/videoStudioE2E.test.ts`) proves that path with its own Node-side
  fake panel rather than the browser client, deliberately.
- Real residual risk, stated precisely: an agent `video_studio transition` command is
  unreachable in a real browser session today because no web code subscribes to the task
  stream. It stays latent only because both vendored dists are absent
  (`electron/filmcraft/dist/index.html` and `electron/effectcraft/dist/index.html` both
  missing), so no editor can mount. The moment fc-01 installs either dist, agent effects
  commands will return `panel_not_open` / `bridge_unavailable` until someone mounts the
  client. That mount is the fc-02 follow-up, not an fc-09 defect.

**Conclusion:** fc-09's acceptance criteria are met and independently re-verified, all six
gates are green, the branding rule holds, and the one cross-branch hazard (cr-04) is
identified and scoped. No code changes were made during this validation; the working tree is
unchanged apart from this record.
